{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the chief cupbearer did not remember, etc.</b> Meaning: even though he did not forget him at first, he did not remember his name as Joseph had charged him, as it is written (Genesis 40:14): ״זְכַרְתַּנִי.״" "<b>Further,</b> the verse informs us that he forgot him also from his heart. And the intention in this is that because he resolved not to remember him, he was forgotten from his heart — for if there had been in his heart and mind even one side to remembering him, through that he would have been somewhat recalled; rather, because the matter was fully resolved, it was forgotten from him (from his heart). And perhaps <b>and he forgot him</b> further alludes that He [HaShem] caused him to forget from his heart and mind whenever he came to recall him, until the time of the end when HaShem remembered Joseph and recalled him. Or perhaps in saying <b>and he forgot him</b> it alludes in this manner: and he forgot — but the Holy One, blessed be He, did not forget him, and recalled him for good — ״וַיְהִי מִקֵּץ,״ etc., and then the chief cupbearer remembered him against his will." "<b>End of the portion of Vayeshev</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:23.687919019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}